# BFF

- Hono BFF is the browser's only backend; Platform calls live in `packages/platform`.
- Keep transport in Platform adapters and product decisions/mapping in domain use cases.
- Validate request, response, environment, and external-service boundaries with Zod.
- Use actual known Platform contracts only; never invent endpoints or fields.
- Map Platform failures into stable application errors and safe responses.
- Derive player identity from the authenticated session/token when possible; do not trust a browser player ID.
- Never return Platform JWTs to browser JavaScript.
- Never log secrets, cookies, JWTs, signatures, passwords, payment credentials, or unnecessary personal data.
- Do not add EveryMatrix, `platformSource`, brand branching, or compatibility DTOs.
- CI tests must mock external traffic and must never call Platform stage.
